`Stack::pop_up_to` searched the whole open-element stack for every end tag,
so an end tag with no matching open element cost O(open elements). The
stack gets deep whenever a document leaves elements open in the
tokenizer's view (omitted </p>, </li>, </td> -- valid HTML), and each stray
or mis-nested end tag then walks all of it: 100k `<p></q>` pairs took 12 s.
Keep a per-name count of open elements and dismiss end tags whose name is
not open at all without touching the stack.

